		<IRequirement type="e">
			<_id type="a">GUID a95a86ea-6185-4ce1-a329-43ab7a9a7a75</_id>
			<_myState type="a">8192</_myState>
			<_name type="a">Authentication</_name>
			<_modifiedTimeWeak type="a">1.2.1990::0:0:0</_modifiedTimeWeak>
			<_description type="p"><IDescription type="e">
				<_text type="a">Authentication consists of entering 4 digits and comparing them with the password</_text>
			</IDescription>
			</_description>
			<_modifiedTime type="a">6.2.2026::10:14:4</_modifiedTime>
		</IRequirement>
		<IRequirement type="e">
			<_id type="a">GUID cb6b0a6a-36ba-41f2-bd06-d9e61bd1d294</_id>
			<_myState type="a">8192</_myState>
			<_name type="a">Collision dewtection</_name>
			<_modifiedTimeWeak type="a">1.2.1990::0:0:0</_modifiedTimeWeak>
			<_description type="p"><IDescription type="e">
				<_text type="a">Collision detection%0D
Collision detection should take place in each period (iteration) of the gate movement and consists in counting by the infrared receiver the pulss sent by infrared transmitter.%0D
1. If the number of pulses received and send differ significantly, send an appropriate signal to the Controller, which should stop the drive%0D
2. Otherwise, keep moving</_text>
			</IDescription>
			</_description>
			<_modifiedTime type="a">6.2.2026::10:29:27</_modifiedTime>
		</IRequirement>
		<IRequirement type="e">
			<_id type="a">GUID 295505b9-9688-4f07-8671-d64c7b6af8c3</_id>
			<_myState type="a">8192</_myState>
			<_name type="a">Firmware</_name>
			<_modifiedTimeWeak type="a">1.2.1990::0:0:0</_modifiedTimeWeak>
			<_description type="p"><IDescription type="e">
				<_text type="a">Firmaware update</_text>
			</IDescription>
			</_description>
			<_modifiedTime type="a">6.2.2026::10:15:9</_modifiedTime>
		</IRequirement>
		<IRequirement type="e">
			<_id type="a">GUID fb3eda7c-f2ac-4829-849b-8b2fa655cf18</_id>
			<_myState type="a">8192</_myState>
			<_name type="a">Movement</_name>
			<_modifiedTimeWeak type="a">1.2.1990::0:0:0</_modifiedTimeWeak>
			<_description type="p"><IDescription type="e">
				<_text type="a">Movement%0D
The transition to the gate movement in the given direction rquires the following steps: %0D
1.Turn on the collision detector.%0D
2. Optional activation of the signalling lamp.%0D
3. Turning on the gate drive.%0D
During the movement taking place in a given direction, the following actions should be repeated every fixed period of time:%0D
1. Send a signal about the travelled distance to the Controller.%0D
2. Check the occurence of a collision and if the collision detector signals it, stop the gate movement.%0D
3. If the signalling option is active, flash the lamp.</_text>
			</IDescription>
			</_description>
			<_modifiedTime type="a">6.2.2026::10:24:51</_modifiedTime>
		</IRequirement>
